body:
True, I missed that use of `dtype` further. Though inside the `sanitize_array` if data is Series then data is cast into numpy array (since `hasattr(Series, "__array__")` is true) and then `sanitize_array` is being called again, then it goes into `_try_cast`, [link](https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas/blob/d6c9941b730855aaa03fd38f0d1216140f90e1ec/pandas/core/construction.py#L789-L793).

```python
    if dtype == object:
        if not is_ndarray:
            subarr = construct_1d_object_array_from_listlike(arr)
            return subarr
        return ensure_wrapped_if_datetimelike(arr).astype(dtype, copy=copy)
```

I agree that this should be considered a bug as current behavior is more like "dtype might be ignored". My last change should be reverted I suppose.
